{"authored" [{"question" "q-10974" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that\n\n$$\n\\frac{7x-37}{(5-3x)(2x+3)}=\\frac{A}{(5-3x)}+\\frac{B}{(2x+3)},\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ and $B$ are real constants, calculate $A+B.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13947700/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d6b5fa4b362496b1d981f4b51c24f887417b886c4e081e5e4bd906d8c4777b1" "basis" 541 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13947700/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10974" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7x-37}{(5-3x)(2x+3)}=\\frac{A}{(5-3x)}+\\frac{B}{(2x+3)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(5-3x)(2x+3)$ gives\n\n$$\n7x-37=A(2x+3)+B(5-3x).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{3}{2}$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(-\\frac{3}{2})-37 & =A(2(-\\frac{3}{2})+3)+B(5-3(-\\frac{3}{2})) \\\\ \\frac{-21-74}{2} & =B(\\frac{10+9}{2}) \\\\ \\frac{-95}{2} & =B(\\frac{19}{2}) \\\\ B & =\\frac{-95}{19} \\\\ B & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=\\frac{5}{3}$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7(\\frac{5}{3})-37 & =A(2(\\frac{5}{3})+3)+B(5-3(\\frac{5}{3})) \\\\ \\frac{35-111}{3} & =A(\\frac{10+9}{3}) \\\\ A & =\\frac{-76}{19} \\\\ A & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\nA+B=-4+(-5)=-4-5=-9.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13947700/state.json" "file_sha256" "6d6b5fa4b362496b1d981f4b51c24f887417b886c4e081e5e4bd906d8c4777b1" "basis" 541 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13947700/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-10974" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/1394770