oblem" "value" "Express $\\dfrac{2x^2+5x+7}{(x+2)(x-3)(x+1)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13947700/example-502.json" "file_sha256" "2c6f613e1ad1cdfd66ce4201940b3807dffd8b35b225cf7e111abd8d7eb99114" "basis" 541 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13947700/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{12x+12}{(x-3)(x-1)(x+5)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959324/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4e9b988c1f38885c97e4e5d7ff2d5de0d972fbc7ccbe17310ac3eec99db1173" "basis" 640 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959324/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12x+12}{(x-3)(x-1)(x+5)} & =\\frac{A}{(x-3)}+\\frac{B}{(x-1)}+\\frac{C}{(x+5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-3)(x-1)(x+5)$ gives\n\n$$\n12x+12=A(x-1)(x+5)+B(x-3)(x+5)+C(x-3)(x-1).\n$$\n\nFor $x=3$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12(3)+12 & =A(3-1)(3+5) \\\\  & \\,+B(3-3)(3+5) \\\\  & \\,+C(3-3)(3-1) \\\\ 36+12 & =A(2)(8) \\\\ A & =\\frac{48}{16} \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=1$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12(1)+12 & =A(1-1)(1+5) \\\\  & \\,+B(1-3)(1+5) \\\\  & \\,+C(1-3)(1-1) \\\\ 12+12 & =B(-2)(6) \\\\ B & =\\frac{24}{-12} \\\\ B & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-5$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12(-5)+12 & =A(-5-1)(-5+5) \\\\  & \\,+B(-5-3)(-5+5) \\\\  & \\,+C(-5-3)(-5-1) \\\\ -60+12 & =C(-8)(-6) \\\\ C & =\\frac{-48}{48} \\\\ C & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{12x+12}{(x-3)(x-1)(x+5)}=\\frac{3}{(x-3)}-\\frac{2}{(x-1)}-\\frac{1}{(x+5)}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959324/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4e9b988c1f38885c97e4e5d7ff2d5de0d972fbc7ccbe17310ac3eec99db1173" "basis" 640 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959324/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959324/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7e2f0edb9809eb216986571ef99ef51b1a93d261b88ea1b5b1e74294deeed33b" "basis" 640 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959324/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69751" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959324/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4e9b988c1f38885c97e4e5d7ff2d5de0d972fbc7ccbe17310ac3eec99db1173" "basis" 640 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959324/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69751" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{(x-3)}+\\frac{3}{(x-1)}+\\frac{2}{(x+5)}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959324/state.json" "file_sha256" "a4e9b988c1f38885c97e4e5d7ff2d5de0d972fbc7ccbe17310ac3eec99db1173" "basis" 640 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959324/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-69751" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{(x-3)}+\\frac{4}{(x-1)}-\\frac{1}{(x+5)}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/D