2x+1)(x+1)+C(2x+1)(x+5).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-\\frac{1}{2}$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+55(-\\frac{1}{2})+19 & =A(-\\frac{1}{2}+5)(-\\frac{1}{2}+1) \\\\  & +B(2(-\\frac{1}{2})+1)(-\\frac{1}{2}+1) \\\\  & +C(2(-\\frac{1}{2})+1)(-\\frac{1}{2}+5) \\\\ 4-\\frac{55}{2}+19 & =A(\\frac{9}{4}) \\\\ \\frac{46-55}{2} & =A(\\frac{9}{4}) \\\\ A & =\\frac{-36}{18} \\\\ A & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-5$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16(-5)^{2}+55(-5)+19 & =A(-5+5)(-5+1) \\\\  & \\,+B(2(-5)+1)(-5+1) \\\\  & +C(2(-5)+1)(-5+5) \\\\ 400-275+19 & =B((-9)(-4)) \\\\ B & =\\frac{144}{36} \\\\ B & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-1$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}16(-1)^{2}+55(-1)+19 & =A(-1+5)(-1+1) \\\\  & \\,+B(2(-1)+1)(-1+1) \\\\  & +C(2(-1)+1)(-1+5) \\\\ 16-55+19 & =C(-4) \\\\ C & =\\frac{-20}{-4} \\\\ C & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{16{x}^{2}+55x+19}{(2x+1)(x+5)(x+1)}=-\\frac{2}{(2x+1)}+\\frac{4}{(x+5)}+\\frac{5}{(x+1)}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038435/state.json" "file_sha256" "86471dc7c39eb5dce9ae750fdcefc742cee98557ce3d97cf06e7b933d036aebf"} {"question" "q-10981" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038435/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3e9b16d30bb8a5be10cc9bbaf6c5a3d7b0db2ba26e54c2f941890788bf70d0c5"} {"question" "q-10981" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038435/state.json" "file_sha256" "86471dc7c39eb5dce9ae750fdcefc742cee98557ce3d97cf06e7b933d036aebf"} {"question" "q-10981" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{(2x+1)}+\\frac{6}{(x+5)}-\\frac{3}{(x+1)}"] ["math" "-\\frac{2}{(2x+1)}+\\frac{4}{(x+5)}+\\frac{5}{(x+1)}"] ["math" "-\\frac{4}{(2x+1)}+\\frac{7}{(x+5)}+\\frac{4}{(x+1)}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{(2x+1)}+\\frac{3}{(x+5)}-\\frac{2}{(x+1)}"] ["math" "\\frac{6}{(2x+1)}+\\frac{2}{(x+5)}-\\frac{11}{(x+1)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038435/state.json" "file_sha256" "86471dc7c39eb5dce9ae750fdcefc742cee98557ce3d97cf06e7b933d036aebf"} {"question" "q-10981" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{2}{(2x+1)}+\\frac{4}{(x+5)}+\\frac{5}{(x+1)}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038435/state.json" "file_sha256" "86471dc7c39eb5dce9ae750fdcefc742cee98557ce3d97cf06e7b933d036aebf"} {"question" "q-69751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\frac{12x+12}{(x-3)(x-1)(x+5)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038435/state.json" "file_sha256" "86471dc7c39eb5dce9ae750fdcefc742cee98557ce3d97cf06e7b933d036aebf"} {"question" "q-69751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A,$ $B$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{12x+12}{(x-3)(x-1)(x+5)} & =\\frac{A}{(x-3)}+\\frac{B}{(x-1)}+\\frac{C}{(x+5)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x-3)(x-1)(x+5)$ gives\n\n$$\n12x+12=A(x-1)(x+5)+B(x-3)(x+5)+C(x-3)(x-1).\n$$\n\nFor $x=3$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12(3)+12 & =A(3-1)(3+5) \\\\  & \\,+B(3-3)(3+5) \\\\  & \\,+C(3-3)(3-1) \\\\ 36+12 & =A(2)(8) \\\\ A & =\\frac{48}{16} \\\\ A & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=1$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12(1)+12 & =A(1-1)(1+5) \\\\  & \\,+B(1-3)(1+5) \\\\  & \\,+C(1-3)(1-1) \\\\ 12+12 & =B(-2)(6) \\\\ B & =\\frac{24}{-12} \\\\ B & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-5$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12(-5)+12 & =A(-5-1)(-5+5) \\\\  & \\,+B(-5-3)(-5+5) \\\\  & \\,+C(-5-3)(-5-1) \\\\ -60+12 & =C(-8)(-6) \\\\ C & =\\frac{-48}{48} \\\\ C & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\frac{12x+12}{(x-3)(x-1)(x+5)}=\\frac{3}{(x-3)}-\\frac{2}{(x-1)}-\\frac{1}{(x+5)}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038435/state.json" "file_sha256" "86471dc7c39eb5dce9ae750fdcefc742cee98557ce3d97cf06e7b933d036aebf"} {"question" "q-69751" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038435/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3e9b16d30bb8a5be10cc9bbaf6c5a3d7b0db2ba26e54c2f941890788bf70d0c5"} {"question" "q-69751" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038435/state.json" "file_sha256" "86471dc7c39eb5dce9ae750fdcefc742cee98557ce3d97cf06e7b933d036aebf"} {"question" "q-69751" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{3}{(x-3)}+\\frac{3}{(x-1)}+\\frac{2}{(x+5)}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{(x-3)}+\\frac{4}{(x-1)}-\\frac{1}{(x+5)}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{(x-3)}-\\frac{2}{(x-1)}-\\frac{1}{(x+5)}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{(x-3)}+\\frac{2}{(x-1)}-\\frac{1}{(x+5)}"] ["math" "\\frac{4}{(x-3)}-\\frac{2}{(x-1)}+\\frac{2}{(x+5)}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038435/state.json" "file_sha256" "86471dc7c39eb5dce9ae750fdcefc742cee98557ce3d97cf06e7b933d036aebf"} {"question" "q-69751" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{3}{(x-3)}-\\frac{2}{(x-1)}-\\frac{1}{(x+5)}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038435/state.json" "file_sha256" "86471dc7c39eb5dce9ae750fdcefc742cee98557ce3d97cf06e7b933d036aebf"} {"question" "e-501" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\dfrac{2x-1}{(x+2)(x-3)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038435/example-501.json" "file_sha256" "9d4a91770633e9c5c60cb7fb3d9c206a2c233cf026f5f1366c7a99d0ec8b16e3"} {"question" "e-501" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x-1}{(x+2)(x-3)} = \\dfrac{A}{(x+2)} +\\dfrac{B}{(x-3)}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above expression through by $(x+2)(x-3)$ gives\n\n$$\n2x-1= A(x-3)+B(x+2).\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-2$ gets rid of the $B$ term and allows us to solve for $A.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-2)-1 & =A(-2-3)+B(-2+2) \\\\ -5 & =A(-5)+B(0) \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=3$ gets rid of the $A$ term and allows us to solve for $B.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(3)-1 & =A(3-3)+B(3+2) \\\\ 5 & =A(0)+B(5) \\\\ B & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKnowing that $A=1$ and $B=1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x-1}{(x+2)(x-3)} = \\dfrac{1}{(x+2)} +\\dfrac{1}{(x-3)}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038435/example-501.json" "file_sha256" "9d4a91770633e9c5c60cb7fb3d9c206a2c233cf026f5f1366c7a99d0ec8b16e3"} {"question" "e-502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Express $\\dfrac{2x^2+5x+7}{(x+2)(x-3)(x+1)}$ as a sum of partial fractions." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038435/example-502.json" "file_sha256" "2c6f613e1ad1cdfd66ce4201940b3807dffd8b35b225cf7e111abd8d7eb99114"} {"question" "e-502" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Our task is to find $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^2+5x+7}{(x+2)(x-3)(x+1)} = \\dfrac{A}{x+2} + \\dfrac{B}{x-3} + \\dfrac{C}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply both sides of the equation by $(x+2)(x-3)(x+1)$ to clear the fractions:\n\n$$\n2x^2+5x+7= A(x-3)(x+1)+B(x+2)(x+1)+C(x+2)(x-3)\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-2$ gets rid of the $B$ and $C$ terms and allows us to solve for $A.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-2)^{2}+5(-2)+7 & =A(-2-3)(-2+1) \\\\ 5 & =A(5) \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=3$ gets rid of the $A$ and $C$ terms and allows us to solve for $B.$ We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(3)^{2}+5(3)+7 & =B(3+2)(3+1) \\\\ 40 & =B(20) \\\\ B & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, plugging in $x=-1$ gets rid of the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C.$ We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(-1)^{2}+5(-1)+7 & =C(-1+2)(-1-3) \\\\ 4 & =C(-4) \\\\ C & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKnowing that $A=1,$ $B=2,$ and $C=-1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^2+5x+7}{(x+2)(x-3)(x+1)} = \\dfrac{1}{x+2} +\\dfrac{2}{x-3} -\\dfrac{1}{x+1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14038435/example-502.json" "file_sha256" "2c6f613e1ad1cdfd66ce4201940b3807dffd8b35b225cf7e111abd8d7eb99114"}] "usage" {"q-10974" [] "q-10989" [] "e-502" [] "e-501" [] "q-10972" [] "q-69751" [] "q-350930" [] "q-10981" []} "basis" 1307 "retractions" [[17592186096865 :question/problem "> A calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nExpress $(-2x^{2} + 21x + 41)/((x + 1)(2 - x)(x + 3))$ as a sum of partial fractions."] [17592186096864 :question/problem "> A calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nExpress $(16x^{2} + 55x + 19)/((2x + 1)(x + 5)(x + 1))$ as a sum of partial fractions."] [17592186096406 :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x-1}{(x+2)(x-3)} = \\dfrac{A}{(x+2)} +\\dfrac{B}{(x-3)}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above expression through by $(x+2)(x-3)$ gives\n\n$$\n2x-1= A(x-3)+B(x+2)\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-2$ gets rid of the $B$ term and allows us to solve for $A$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(-2) - 1 &= A(-2 - 3) + B(-2 + 2) \\\\\n- 5 &= A(-5) + B(0) \\\\\nA &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=3$ gets rid of the $A$ term and allows us to solve for $B$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(3) - 1 &= A(3 - 3) + B(3 + 2) \\\\\n5 &= A(0) + B(5) \\\\\nB &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKnowing that $A=1$ and $B=1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x-1}{(x+2)(x-3)} = \\dfrac{1}{(x+2)} +\\dfrac{1}{(x-3)}\n$$"] [17592186096410 :question/worked-solution "Our task is to find $A$, $B$, and $C$ such that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^2+5x+7}{(x+2)(x-3)(x+1)} = \\dfrac{A}{x+2} + \\dfrac{B}{x-3} + \\dfrac{C}{x+1}\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply both sides of the equation by $(x+2)(x-3)(x+1)$ to clear the fractions:\n\n$$\n2x^2+5x+7= A(x-3)(x+1)+B(x+2)(x+1)+C(x+2)(x-3)\n$$\n\nPlugging in $x=-2$ gets rid of the $B$ and $C$ terms and allows us to solve for $A$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(-2)^{2} + 5(-2) + 7 &= A(-2 - 3)(-2 + 1) \\\\\n5 &= A(5) \\\\\nA &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, plugging in $x=3$ gets rid of the $A$ and $C$ terms and allows us to solve for $B$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(3)^{2} + 5(3) + 7 &= B(3 + 2)(3 + 1) \\\\\n40 &= B(20) \\\\\nB &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, plugging in $x=-1$ gets rid of the $A$ and $B$ terms and allows us to solve for $C$. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(-1)^{2} + 5(-1) + 7 &= C(-1 + 2)(-1 - 3) \\\\\n4 &= C(-4) \\\\\nC &= -1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nKnowing that $A=1$, $B=2$, and $C=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{2x^2+5x+7}{(x+2)(x-3)(x+1)} = \\dfrac{1}{x+2} +\\dfrac{2}{x-3} -\\dfrac{1}{x+1}\n$$"]] "